  "body": "## What changed\nA race in flecs' first-world setup crashed test binaries under load: SIGSEGV in `scripting`, and very likely the earlier one-off SIGABRT in `project_roundtrip`.\n\nflecs keeps its OS API (malloc, free, abort, clock hooks) in one process-global C struct, filled in without a lock on the first world.\n- `flecs_ecs::ecs_os_api::ensure_initialized` (flecs_ecs 0.2.2) claims the first fill under a mutex, but writes the struct after releasing it.\n- `ecs_mini`, the C side of `World::new`, copies the struct and writes it back.\n- A second thread creating its first world at that moment can copy a half-written struct. `ecs_mini` then aborts on `ECS_MISSING_OS_API` (SIGABRT) or later calls a NULL hook (SIGSEGV).\n\n**Fix:** `crates/app/src/world.rs`. `new_world()`, the only place a `World` is built (a grep finds no other `World::new` / `World::default`), now runs `ecs_os_api::ensure_initialized` once behind a `std::sync::Once`, before building any world. After that first fill, flecs marks the API initialised and later constructions only read it. No `unsafe`, and no change to the vendored C.\n\n## Readings\n- **Stack**, captured with lldb from a reproduced crash: `abort <- ecs_mini.cold.1 <- ecs_mini (flecs.c:21288, ecs_os_has_heap check) <- ecs_init <- World::default <- camcraft_app::world::new_world <- script::Env::fresh <- script::run`. At the same moment a sibling test thread was inside `ecs_set_hooks_id` building another world.\n- **Scripting suite**, 8 parallel copies, `--test-threads=32`: before, 7 crashes in 1200 runs (6 SIGSEGV, 1 SIGABRT); after, 0 in 1600.\n- **`world_init_race` children:** before, 6 crashed in 1920; after, 0 in 3840.\n- **`project_roundtrip`**, 6 × 60 runs at 32 threads: 0 crashes in 360.\n- **Quick gate** (upstream/main merged, clean): app and post green. The remaining reds also fail on upstream main: `swarf_pose_continuity` (fixed by #351) and the GPU headless tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning test\n`crates/app/tests/world_init_race.rs::first_worlds_on_many_threads_never_crash` (gate map `app::world`).\n- It reruns its own binary as 720 child processes in waves of 24, under spinner load.\n- In each child, 32 threads wait at a barrier and then all build their first world. Every child must exit cleanly. It takes about 4 s.\n- It is a stress test: without the fix it fails in roughly 2 runs out of 3.\n\n## Not addressed (possible follow-ups)\n- **Windows:** flecs bumps `ecs_os_api_init_count` without atomics. That is harmless on POSIX (the guarded hooks are NULL), but a lost update on Windows could run `win_fini` early. Never observed.\n- **Stack margin:** a debug script run uses about 950 KB of stack against 2 MiB test threads, so the margin is only about 2x.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/379-scripting-sigsegv.md`.\n\nChangelog: Fixed an intermittent crash (SIGSEGV/SIGABRT) when several threads created their first CamCraft world at once - flecs' OS API is now initialised once before any world (#379)\n\nFixes #379\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
